WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.789 --> 00:00:05.990
We have the latest numbers from last week's
new unemployment claims.

00:00:05.990 --> 00:00:12.080
Three point eight million more people, additional
people have lost their jobs.

00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:15.349
We've been tracking this weekly since the
start of Carone.

00:00:15.349 --> 00:00:19.560
I mean, we always track it weekly, but we've
been looking at numbers this bad since the

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:21.270
start of the virus.

00:00:21.270 --> 00:00:25.410
Some weeks the numbers have been as high as
six point eight million in one week losing

00:00:25.410 --> 00:00:26.619
their jobs.

00:00:26.619 --> 00:00:34.530
This is now a reduction in new claims, 3.8
million more people lost their jobs last week.

00:00:34.530 --> 00:00:37.070
So in total, this is the terrible news.

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:40.510
Thirty million people have now lost their
jobs due to corrupt coronavirus.

00:00:40.510 --> 00:00:45.760
To give you a little context for that number,
before this started, the workforce was believed

00:00:45.760 --> 00:00:51.220
to be one hundred and fifty eight million
in the United States, 1 5 8 million.

00:00:51.220 --> 00:00:54.500
Thirty million is about 19 percent.

00:00:54.500 --> 00:01:02.020
19 percent of all working people have lost
their jobs in the United States in the last

00:01:02.020 --> 00:01:03.739
six or seven weeks.

00:01:03.739 --> 00:01:04.940
This is nightmarish.

00:01:04.940 --> 00:01:09.990
These are numbers that are so outrageous that
eight weeks ago they would have been unimaginable

00:01:09.990 --> 00:01:10.990
numbers.

00:01:10.990 --> 00:01:12.280
The slightly OK news.

00:01:12.280 --> 00:01:15.550
If we're looking for trends, right, like if
we really if we want to find something that's

00:01:15.550 --> 00:01:19.240
slightly OK, news is it's not 6 million every
week.

00:01:19.240 --> 00:01:20.530
It's been diminishing.

00:01:20.530 --> 00:01:24.260
We add 6.6 million people lost their job.

00:01:24.260 --> 00:01:29.790
Get 6.8, then 6.6, 5.2, then 4.4 and now 3.8.

00:01:29.790 --> 00:01:34.720
So hopefully over the next four to six weeks,
we'll see the numbers of new claims continue

00:01:34.720 --> 00:01:35.909
to diminish.

00:01:35.909 --> 00:01:41.780
Eventually, hopefully we will see a net decrease
in the number of people who are not working.

00:01:41.780 --> 00:01:43.119
But this is not going to be quick.

00:01:43.119 --> 00:01:47.210
You know, Trump talks about this V-shaped
recovery that will be as quick or even quicker

00:01:47.210 --> 00:01:48.450
than the decline.

00:01:48.450 --> 00:01:49.920
Doesn't seem like it's going to be that way.

00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:53.520
Many jobs that are being lost are permanent
job losses.

00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:56.110
Many businesses are not going to reopen.

00:01:56.110 --> 00:02:00.189
And what's also becoming completely clear
is that there hasn't been enough stimulus

00:02:00.189 --> 00:02:01.189
from the government.

00:02:01.189 --> 00:02:04.510
We're now well into month number two of this.

00:02:04.510 --> 00:02:05.510
Some states are about.

00:02:05.510 --> 00:02:10.030
I mean, here in Massachusetts, we're very
close to entering month number three.

00:02:10.030 --> 00:02:13.980
And there are still people who have not gotten
their twelve hundred dollar checks.

00:02:13.980 --> 00:02:16.660
And even when they get the twelve hundred,
it's not going to be enough.

00:02:16.660 --> 00:02:18.340
This is going to be a big deal.

00:02:18.340 --> 00:02:23.370
Remember that before this, half the country
couldn't even afford an unexpected four hundred

00:02:23.370 --> 00:02:24.370
dollar expense.

00:02:24.370 --> 00:02:26.269
That was before this.

00:02:26.269 --> 00:02:27.890
Those numbers are going to go way, way up.

00:02:27.890 --> 00:02:30.620
They're gonna get much more ugly as this continues.

00:02:30.620 --> 00:02:32.529
We are going to need more stimulus.

00:02:32.529 --> 00:02:35.829
I would like to also see infrastructure done.

00:02:35.829 --> 00:02:40.980
And I'll talk next week about how much more
stimulus we are likely to need, as well as

00:02:40.980 --> 00:02:43.439
what an infrastructure deal would look like.

00:02:43.439 --> 00:02:48.950
And you know, the thing about Trump is everything
